      "documentConcept": "PD sleep disorders: RBD, insomnia and daytime sleepiness",
      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:dbe246490e3708ce091ee139994202fd1867e14f8c536ed04b13a04aff20fdfa",
      "text": "The cited sources distinguish dream enactment with injury risk, insomnia, and daytime sleepiness in PD. The AASM guideline pairs environmental safety advice with conditional drug options for RBD; clonazepam and immediate-release melatonin have conditional guideline support, while prolonged-release melatonin failed in a small PD trial. Insomnia assessment considers other sleep disorders, and CBT-I evidence in PD is promising but limited by small studies and adherence. NICE describes a medication review, a search for reversible causes and driving precautions for daytime sleepiness. Modafinil has mixed efficacy evidence; CPAP evidence applies to coexisting obstructive sleep apnea. Guideline options and positive pooled findings should retain their evidence limitations.",
